{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Living the Dream", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "I Got Accepted!", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 16, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Passive Voice with Modals", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the passive voice when you want to focus on the receiver of the action, rather than the \u2018doer' of the action. <br/> You can also use <span class=\"strong\">modal verbs</span> in the passive voice. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Sometimes, something must/can/should be done by someone. It that case, we use some <span class=\"strong\">modal verbs</span>. Remember, after a modal verb, <span class=\"italic\">to</span> is not necessary before the main verb. <br> For example: <br> Example: <span class=\"italic\">This lesson must be practiced.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Modal verbs</span> can add meaning connected with <span class=\"underline\">suggestion </span> or <span class=\"underline\">obligation</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Here is the structure of a passive sentence:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + modal verb + be + past participle of the main verb", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">The company <span class=\"strong\">must be sold </span> on your performance.</span>  <br/><span class=\"italic\">Now that you have a new job, you car <span class=\"strong\">has to be fixed</span>.</span>  <br/><span class=\"italic\">The bills <span class=\"strong\">have to be paid</span> by tomorrow.</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" have/has/must\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"(to) be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Your car<br/> The bills\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"has <br/> have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to be <br/> to be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"fixed. <br/> paid by Tuesday.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The employer\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"must\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"sold.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": " I also have some bills that must be paid and a student loan that should be addressed. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The project should be presented next Friday.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " It should be mentioned that I received another text from Boris today.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " What-Clauses and Long Noun Phrases as Subjects", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\"> What-clauses </span> are used to help us focus on a particular part of the sentence and to emphasize what we want to say by introducing it as a relative clause.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">What-clauses</span> are usually linked to the clause that we want to focus on with <span class=\"strong\">is </span> or <span class=\"strong\">was</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">What</span>  I now need <span class=\"strong\">is </span> a new car</span> .<br/> <span class=\"italic\">A new car is <span class=\"strong\">what I </span> now need.</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">What </span> I enjoyed most <span class=\"strong\">was </span> seeing their new office.</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">Seeing their new office <span class=\"strong\">was what </span> I enjoyed most.</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">What-clauses </span> are often used with verbs like <span class=\"strong\">adore</span>, <span class=\"strong\">dislike</span>, <span class=\"strong\">enjoy</span>, <span class=\"strong\">hate</span>, <span class=\"strong\">like</span>, <span class=\"strong\">loathe</span>, <span class=\"strong\">love</span>, <span class=\"strong\">need</span>, <span class=\"strong\">prefer</span>, <span class=\"strong\">want</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">What </span> I <span class=\"strong\">hate </span> most about going to a job interview is the waiting.</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">What </span> I <span class=\"strong\">liked </span> most about their company was the people.</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">What-clauses</span>  are also often used with <span class=\"strong\">does</span>/<span class=\"strong\">do</span>/<span class=\"strong\">did</span> and when we want to give emphasis to the whole sentence, rather than a particular clause.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">The manager interviewed all the salespeople first.</span> <br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">What </span> the manager <span class=\"strong\">did </span> first <span class=\"strong\">was </span> interview all the salespeople. </span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "These sentences are useful in writing where we cannot use intonation for emphasis, but they are also often used in speech.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What I want you to do is to make some goals for this job. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "What I want is a used car.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "What he wanted was to tell me about another editorial assistant job. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "What worries me is that you are new and if Adam doesn't do a good job, it may reflect badly on you.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "pumped up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "motivated; excited", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: That job seminar has me so pumped up right now!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you need to review.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "right out of the gate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "from the beginning ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I think it turned the interviewer off right out of the gate.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to start off on the wrong foot", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to begin in an awkward or unpleasant way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  This interview has started off on the wrong foot. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ideal", "type": "name"}, {"content": "perfect", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Your skills and experience will be an ideal fit for our team.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le16ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sounds like a plan", "type": "name"}, {"content": "that's a good idea", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: <br/> <span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Let's meet Thursday? <br/><span class=\"stro